{"id":"graphicnovel","name":"graphicnovel","aliases":[],"caption":"A semantic LaTeX class for graphic-novel and comic scripts","authors":[{"id":"bronte","active":true}],"copyright":[{"owner":"Tom Bronte","year":"2026"}],"license":"lppl1.3c","version":{"number":"0.5.0","date":""},"descriptions":[{"language":null,"text":"<p> This package uses the working language of comics: stories,\n      eras, pages, panels, locations, shots, action, dialogue,\n      captions, and sound effects. Consistency matters as much to the\n      artist as to the writer.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p> The <i>reference bible<\u002fi> is authoritative. Characters,\n      places, persistent objects, expressions, tells, and continuity\n      notes are defined once, then referenced throughout the script.\n      Era-specific appearances describe how people, places, and\n      objects change over time. The class checks script references\n      against the bible definitions during compilation.\n    <\u002fp>\n  <p>\n      What it provides:\n    <\u002fp>\n  <ul>\n    <li>\n\tA reference bible for characters, places, objects, and continuity notes.\n      <\u002fli>\n    <li>\n\tEra-specific appearances, named expressions, and behavioural tells.\n      <\u002fli>\n    <li>\n\tStories, vignettes, comic pages, panels, and double-page spreads.\n      <\u002fli>\n    <li>\n\tPage layouts expressed as panel counts by row, such as \\pageLayout{2,1,2}.\n      <\u002fli>\n    <li>\n\t  Automated page and panel counters so you don't have to worry.\n\t<\u002fli>\n    <li>\n\t  Separate directions for background (\\location), composition (\\shot), and\n\t  foreground activity (\\action).\n\t<\u002fli>\n    <li>\n\t  Dialogue, balloon-position notes, captions, sound effects, and production\n\t  notes.\n\t<\u002fli>\n    <li>\n\t  A compact option for proofreading without forced page breaks.\n\t<\u002fli>\n  <\u002ful>\n  <p>\n        GraphicNovel produces a script and reference material for collaborators. It\n        does not draw panels or generate finished comic artwork, but\n        at least everyone will be singing from the same hymn sheet.\n      <\u002fp>"}],"documentation":[{"language":null,"details":"Package documentation","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/graphicnovel/graphicnovel-manual.pdf"},{"language":null,"details":"Readme","href":"ctan:/macros/latex/contrib/graphicnovel/README.md"}],"home":"https://craftsyntax.uk/","support":"https://github.com/craftsyntax-uk/GraphicNovel/issues","announce":"https://craftsyntax.substack.com","bugs":"https://github.com/craftsyntax-uk/GraphicNovel/issues","repository":"https://github.com/craftsyntax-uk/GraphicNovel","development":"https://github.com/craftsyntax-uk/GraphicNovel","ctan":{"path":"/macros/latex/contrib/graphicnovel","file":true},"miktex":"graphicnovel","texlive":"graphicnovel","topics":["class","drama-script"]}